---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const base = '/participation-registration-entry/20261107-01/';
type Row = { county: string; accepted_cohort: number; post_2024_registration: number;
	positive_2024_nc_history: number; no_2024_nc_history_found: number;
	positive_history_share_of_post_registration_pct: number };
const analysis: { rows: Row[] } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}summary.json`, 'utf8'));
const integer = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
---

<section id="participation-registration-entry" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="registration-entry-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Administrative participation evidence · Selected early/mail cohorts</p>
		<h2 id="registration-entry-title">A new registration date does not mean a first-time voter</h2>
		<p>In these two North Carolina counties, thousands of accepted 2026 early/mail voters
			with a registration date after the 2024 election already have
			<strong>positive 2024 North Carolina general-election history</strong>.
			The current record's registration date is not a first-ever registration date.</p>
	</header>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Registration dates and positive prior North Carolina participation">
		<table>
			<caption>Current-record registration dates after November 5, 2024, through November 3, 2026.
				Percentages below are among that selected date group, not all voters.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">County</th><th scope="col">Accepted early/mail cohort</th>
				<th scope="col">Registration after 2024</th><th scope="col">Of those: positive 2024 NC history</th>
				<th scope="col">Of those: no 2024 NC history found</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{analysis.rows.map(row => <tr data-registration-county={row.county}>
				<th scope="row">{row.county === 'WAKE' ? 'Wake' : 'Mecklenburg'}</th>
				<td data-registration-count="accepted_cohort">{integer(row.accepted_cohort)}</td>
				<td data-registration-count="post_2024_registration">{integer(row.post_2024_registration)}</td>
				<td><span data-registration-count="positive_2024_nc_history">{integer(row.positive_2024_nc_history)}</span>
					<br /><span data-registration-positive-share>{row.positive_history_share_of_post_registration_pct.toFixed(1)}% of date group</span></td>
				<td><span data-registration-count="no_2024_nc_history_found">{integer(row.no_2024_nc_history_found)}</span>
					<br />National participation unresolved</td>
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p><strong>No first-time-voter estimate.</strong> Movers and re-registrations can have later
		registration dates despite earlier participation. No NC history match does not establish
		no 2024 vote elsewhere. Neither group is labeled new to voting.</p>
	<p><strong>Not final turnout or counted ballots.</strong> This is the source's accepted
		early/mail cohort only, not all Election Day voters. Registration and history files were
		last modified November 2; accepted records November 6. These snapshots are not one
		synchronized final electorate. No candidate choice, persuasion or staying home is inferred.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Scope, source controls and complete reproduction</summary>
		<p>The <a href="https://www.ncsbe.gov/results-data/voter-registration-data">NCSBE registration files</a>
			supply the current record's <code>registr_dt</code>. We link the already reviewed, frozen
			accepted early/mail cohort to
			<a href="https://www.ncsbe.gov/results-data/voter-history-data">statewide NC general-election history</a>,
			not just history in the current county. Every record for an ambiguous registration or
			accepted identifier is excluded, never arbitrarily deduplicated.
			Missing and all other registration dates remain outside the selected date interval.</p>
		<p>Source URLs, acquisition and modification dates, full native hashes, private source-control
			proof hashes, both selected county rows, both history outcomes, full accepted-cohort
			controls, code, tests and results are included. Offline reproduction starts from the
			complete selected aggregates; it does not recreate private native linkage. No individual
			records, fine joint cells, identities or scores are redistributed. These two counties
			are not estimates for North Carolina or the country; no demographic allocation is made.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete selected registration-date analysis + inputs + code + results (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}summary.json`} download>Registration-date counts + qualifications (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Registration-date archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-registration-entry { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
